    <sys:String x:Key="EmulationPage.Emulation.ForceAudioHaptics.Description">Derive vibration from the forwarded audio instead of the game's own haptics. The haptic strength slider always applies to audio-based haptics. Only applies to DualSense emulation over Bluetooth.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="EmulationPage.Emulation.ForwardHaptics">Forwarded Haptic Strength</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="EmulationPage.Emulation.ForwardHaptics.Description">Strength of the vibration generated from forwarded desktop sounds. Only applies while the virtual audio output is selected as the default playback device.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="EmulationPage.Emulation.ForwardVolume">Forwarded Audio Volume</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="EmulationPage.Emulation.ForwardVolume.Description">Volume of the desktop sounds forwarded to the controller. Only applies while the virtual audio output is selected as the default playback device.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="EmulationPage.Emulation.Mode">Emulation Mode</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="EmulationPage.Emulation.Mode.Description">Creates a virtual controller that mirrors this controller's input to the host. Feedback (rumble, lightbar, triggers) is forwarded back. These settings are stored per controller.</sys:String>
